      {
        "@type": "Place",
        "description": "The tropical montane forest is in the northern part of Borneo, near the border between the state of Sabah, Malaysia and Kalimantan, Indonesia (4\u207023 - 27\u2019N, 115\u207042 - 47\u2019E). Local villagers and authorities have modified the forest for shifting cultivation and commercial timber logging. Two LiDAR scanning sites captured the human-modified montane forest: Site 1 (2.67 km x 8 km) is near the village of Long Mio, and Site 2 (2 km x 6 km) comprises primarily forest compartments of a forestry company. The coordinates of plots are included as a shape file in the data package.",
